# Example .envrc for local development (direnv). Copy to `.envrc` — which is
# gitignored — and adjust. This template exists so the real `.envrc` never needs
# to hold secrets in the repo working tree (#831).
#
# Two rules this layout enforces:
#
#   1. NO ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here. This repo runs Claude via subscription OAuth
#      (~/.claude/.credentials.json), never a metered API key. Setting one makes
#      every agent/SDK/CLI run silently bill the API — the exact failure the rule
#      exists to prevent. The `.envrc` actively `unset`s it.
#
#   2. Third-party API keys live in a file OUTSIDE the repo, so a stray
#      `git add -f` or a tooling change can't promote live secrets into this
#      public repo. `.envrc` sources that file; the keys never touch the tree.

use nix

# Keep real keys here (0600), outside the repo. Override the path with
# AIFACTORY_SECRETS_ENV if you use e.g. an agenix-decrypted location.
#   $ mkdir -p ~/.config/aifactory && touch ~/.config/aifactory/secrets.env
#   $ chmod 600 ~/.config/aifactory/secrets.env
# then put your `export OPENAI_API_KEY=...` etc. lines in it (NOT ANTHROPIC).
_aif_secrets="${AIFACTORY_SECRETS_ENV:-${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/aifactory/secrets.env}"
if [ -f "$_aif_secrets" ]; then
  # shellcheck disable=SC1090
  source "$_aif_secrets"
fi
unset _aif_secrets

# Belt-and-braces: drop any ANTHROPIC_API_KEY inherited from a parent shell so
# the SDK/CLI falls back to OAuth without needing `env -u ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`.
unset ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
